Alert Tracker Automation - User Guide

Overview

This Power Automate flow automatically processes two email reports and consolidates the data into a SharePoint Alert Tracker list. It captures users flagged for geofencing violations and enriches their records with device/location information.

How It Works

The flow monitors two email sources:

The Geofencing Freeze New Devices email contains identifiers of users who triggered a geofencing alert. This creates NEW items in the Alert Tracker and sets the Title field (unique identifier).

The Monitored Devices email contains detailed device and location information such as IP, city, country, etc. This ENRICHES existing items in the Alert Tracker by matching on the Title field and adding the extra data.

Flow Logic

Part 1: Freeze Email Processing

The flow gets emails from the Geofencing Freeze folder, extracts the CSV attachment, decodes it, and splits it into rows. For each row it checks if the row is not empty (Condition 2), then checks if the Title already exists in SharePoint for de-duplication. If the Title is new, it creates an item in the Alert Tracker. If it already exists, it skips it.

Part 2: Monitored Devices Processing

The flow gets emails from the Monitored Devices folder, extracts the CSV attachment, decodes it, and splits it into rows. For each row it checks if the row is not empty (Condition 1), then gets the matching item from SharePoint by Title. It checks if a match exists (Condition 3). If a match is found, it checks if Violation_Country is empty (Condition 4). If true (first enrichment), it sets BOTH Violation_Country AND Current_Country. If false (already enriched), it sets ONLY Current_Country. If no match is found, it skips the row.

Country Tracking Logic

The Violation_Country field captures where the user was when FIRST flagged. This is only set on the first enrichment and never changes after that.

The Current_Country field captures where the user is NOW. This updates every time the flow runs if new data comes in.

This allows you to track if someone has moved countries since their original violation.

SharePoint Columns

The Alert Tracker list should have these columns:

    Title (unique identifier from Freeze CSV)
    Violation_Country
    Current_Country
    Plus any other enrichment fields such as City, IP, etc.

Key Expressions Used

Empty Row Check:
greater(length(split(items('Apply_to_each'), ',')), 1)

Match Found Check:
length(body('Get_items')?['value']) is greater than 0

Violation Country Empty Check:
empty(body('Get_items')?['value'][0]?['Violation_Country'])

Extract CSV Column Value:
if(greater(length(split(items('Apply_to_each'), ',')), 1), split(items('Apply_to_each'), ',')[X], '')

Replace X with the column index (0-based counting).

CSV Column Mapping

Index [0] is the first column. Index [1] is the second column. Index [10] is the country field. Update these index numbers if your CSV column order changes.

Troubleshooting

If you see "Invalid ID" or "Update Item failed" errors, this usually means no matching Title was found in SharePoint. Condition 3 should catch this by checking if length is greater than 0.

If empty rows are causing errors, Condition 1 and Condition 2 should filter these out. Make sure they check that the split length is greater than 1.

If data is not enriching, check that the identifier in the Monitored Devices CSV exactly matches the Title in the Alert Tracker. Look for extra spaces or formatting differences.

Making Changes

To change which CSV column maps to which SharePoint field, find the Update Item or Create Item action, edit the expression split(items('Apply_to_each'), ',')[X], and change X to the correct column index.

To add a new SharePoint column, first add the column to the SharePoint list, then edit the Update Item or Create Item action, and add the new field mapped to the correct CSV column.

Testing

Send a test email with a CSV attachment to the appropriate mailbox. Run the flow manually or wait for the trigger. Check the SharePoint list for new or updated items. Check the flow run history for any errors.
